1) fuckZHS — https://github.com/VermiIIi0n/fuckZHS
   License: MIT License, Copyright (c) VermiIIi0n

   This project's API layer (course tree / progress reporting / quiz answering)
   is implemented by calling into "fuckZHS" at runtime. **No upstream source
   code is vendored in this repository**: users install the engine separately
   and point `engine_home` (or ZHS_ENGINE_HOME) at it, so upstream code is not
   redistributed here.

   If you ever vendor upstream files into this repository, you MUST keep the
   upstream MIT notice above (e.g. `third_party/fuckZHS/LICENSE`) and list it in
   this section.

   Upstream is a single-author project; the polite thing to do — and what this
   project does — is to credit it in README.md and pin a specific commit/tag so
   builds stay reproducible.

2) Python dependencies (fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, websocket-client, requests,
   openai, tiktoken, pycryptodome, pillow) are installed from PyPI under their
   own licenses and are not redistributed in this repository.

3) "zhihuishu" / 智慧树 is a trademark of its respective owner. This project is
   an unofficial client-side tool: it is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
   supported by the platform.
